WEBVTT

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.900
Excuse me. Where's Homura-san?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.220
Looks like she already left for band practice.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.190
Oh...

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.550
"First Love Sommelier"...

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.430
<i>Two months to go until
the All-Japan qualifiers.</i>

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.520
<i>We've decided on our performance piece,
and it feels like things are starting to get real.</i>

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.000
Here's your lunch.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.160
You're making lunch for Kamijou-kun
as well, Homura-san?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.020
Yeah. As his pay for tutoring me before the exams.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.200
I thought the deal was that
you'd make him dinner.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.820
It was, but my mum's away this week.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.670
She's gone to take care of my dad, who caught
a cold while living in another town for work.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.560
Wait, so you're home alone right now?

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.070
Jeez. Serves you right for eating too fast.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.420
What kind of rice balls are these?

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.260
Mixed vegetable.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.440
Unbelievable!

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.030
I make them myself.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.800
The filling is canned mackerel.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.810
Full of DHA that'll make me
at least a little smarter.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.130
Kaiyuu, please share them with Chika-chan!

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.520
Joo wad?! Joo needem morean I do!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.280
Less talking with your mouth full, more eating.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.030
The choir will be using this room from 1PM.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.980
We start practice at 3:30PM today.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:04.960
Until then, you're free to take a break
or practise by yourself.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:05.530
Okay!

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.320
Maren, would you like to
rehearse the F part together?

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.030
Sure.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.200
Count me in.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.830
Would you like to join us, Kamijou-kun?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.010
Yeah. How about you, Chika-chan?

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.720
Oh, uh, I'll practise alone.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.250
I want to get used to the score.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.790
You should just memorise it.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.700
Yeah.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.520
Where should we rehearse, by the way?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.270
I looked all over for you.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.100
Serizawa-san?

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:42.680
You have to play with the alto sax here,
so make sure you keep an ear out for it.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.020
Do you want me to teach you more?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.320
You'll do that for me?

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.240
I don't mind helping you out.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.740
I'll even give you a
one-day lesson, if you like.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.500
What's the catch?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.490
My aunt is here at school right now,

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:00.830
having an interview with a shady guy
who calls himself the First Love Sommelier.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.880
I want to save her, so come with me.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.560
I didn't get any of that.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.090
That doesn't mean you have to drag <i>me</i> into it.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.190
I have an aunt who runs
a general store in Australia.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:18.020
She'll move back to Japan once I graduate,
and the two of us are to live together.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.330
You're moving out, Nao-chan?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.110
I don't want to stay in that house anymore.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.780
I see...

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:24.790
And?
I see...

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.070
And?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:32.360
When she visited a month ago, she hired
a local detective agency to look for someone.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.330
Who?

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.100
Her first love.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.870
Is your aunt single?

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:42.210
Yeah. Anyway, that investigation
has been completed already.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:46.240
She found out where her first love
lived over a decade ago,

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.550
but his current whereabouts are unknown.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.930
Now we get to the
heart of the problem.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:56.840
The sole heir of the detective agency
she hired sent her a provocative postcard.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.350
"Researching methods to verify
the authenticity of first loves"?

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.560
"First Love Sommelier,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.860
Asagiri Tohru."

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.160
You know of him?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.260
I think he's President Katagiri's classmate.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.460
Even Hinohara-san, the student council
president, pays him special attention.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.660
Oddball incoming.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.870
He's an oddball.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.760
Knew it.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.080
Can you hear over all the noise?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.040
I can handle this much.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.290
What is this First Love Research Club?

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:27.140
Asagiri considers first love as nothing
but material to be researched.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.890
Stay away from him, or he'll violate
every last private detail of your first love.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.290
You seem awfully well-informed.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.700
What? I-I guess.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.060
Where is this club?

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.890
The old school building's ground floor,

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:45.640
where the drama club, the inventor club,
and the geological research club are also located.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.690
Also known as the Teenager Safari Park.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.110
Thanks.

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:55.250
Asagiri's one of the
sharpest tools in the shed.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.830
If Serizawa goes at him head-on,
it'll end in tears for her.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:01.680
Let's go!

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.520
So this is the Teenager Safari Park...

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.200
It was just a figure of speech.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:15.080
Yo! Say hi to Kaiyuu for me.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.240
Tell him to come hang out sometimes.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.030
What's with that girl?

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.940
If your first love was genuine...

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.860
That'll be a huge load off my mind.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.650
But if it wasn't...

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:35.750
Everything will be buried in the dark once more.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.370
Aunty!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.110
Oh, Naoko.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:43.810
I came because I was worried about you.
Come on, let's leave.

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.670
But, Naoko...

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.500
I'm about to start appraising her first love.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.560
Could you wait outside?

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:52.140
No way.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.110
Is that the First Love Sommelier?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.560
Looks like it.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:00.970
Asagiri-san, do you mind if Naoko
and her friends stay here?

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:03.590
Of course not.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.280
Then, Serizawa Naoko-san...

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.740
Huh? Me?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:12.040
How would you define first love?

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.070
Literally just the first time
you fall in love, I guess?

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.290
What a baby.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:17.960
Th-There, there.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.070
First love is, by nature, always a flashback.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:28.140
This is what allows one to look back on it
and convince themselves it was love.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.310
Not only that, it gets embellished
beyond recognition.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.190
That is why, when they later come
face-to-face with their first love,

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:38.680
they are shocked by the gap
between reality and their memories.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.190
Isn't that how it usually goes with memories?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:45.140
That is exactly why first loves
need to be appraised, don't you think?

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.440
Nope.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.440
By removing the false and exaggerated
elements from the memories,

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.030
we reproduce the exact circumstances
of the time and perform an appraisal.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.860
How, exactly?

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:57.550
Tasting.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.990
We have our clients smell an aroma.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.160
The Proust effect.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.670
The phenomenon where smell
can awaken one's memories.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.040
Bingo.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:11.640
Reproducing that aroma using wisdom
and creativity is the First Love Sommelier's job.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.300
Let's get everything ready, then.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:22.520
I've never heard you talk about your first love.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:30.030
Naoko, there are things you can reveal to
a stranger but not to those important to you.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.120
I can't accept this!

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.550
Though I'm a total stranger...

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.280
I understand what you just said.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:43.830
Pardon me for being too forward, but I daresay
you're not being fair to Naoko-san, your niece.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.770
Aren't you misusing the word "fair" there?

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.130
Let me put it this way, then.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.040
I understand your reasoning,
but it doesn't sit right with me.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.510
You weren't kidding about being too forward, eh?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.510
Is it wrong to help a friend in need?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.560
I'm glad Naoko has such wonderful friends.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.790
Asagiri-san.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:09.640
Do I have time to tell Naoko
and her friends about my first love?

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:14.580
A little, sure. But do you really intend
to give them the whole story?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.200
I'll tell the story as I see fit.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:21.520
Whether you can read
between the lines is up to you.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.490
Okay.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:27.000
I experienced my first love when I was
a nineteen-year-old college student.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.670
That boy and I shared a certain something.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.320
What was it?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.840
Rice balls.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.470
Rice balls?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:50.630
This is a story of a girl who left home for the city
and ended up lost in a deep forest.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:55.350
We stand in firm opposition
of the invasion of dark forces

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:59.370
and demand that our forest
brethren criticise themselves!

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:04.830
We must reach out for the stars
and survive this fight to the death!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:06.750
My fellow forestmen!

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.120
Who are you people?

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.260
We are the Forest Brotherhood.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.760
I'm Venganto, and I'm in
charge of making rice balls.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.670
Forest Brotherhood?

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.480
It's a metaphor, Chika-chan.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:26.350
How many "brothers" were there in total?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.880
Eight.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.680
The birds would leave immediately
after the commotion died down.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:35.190
The girl believed she'd be able
to get out of the forest someday

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.530
and started making rice balls for them.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:40.580
Hey!

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:42.620
Step on it, you useless hacks!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.450
Got it!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:44.660
Dimwitted fools.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:52.250
You take the rice balls to the birds,
and I'll take them to the Brotherhood.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.720
Thank you, Venganto.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.550
I'll give you a name too.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.140
Purastelo.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.640
That's your name from now on.

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.000
Purastelo...

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:12.190
He was very knowledgeable and
taught her a great many things.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:18.030
To the girl, he was the first boy
she'd spent a long time with.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.700
So this Venganto was your first love?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.230
Yes.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:23.870
He was a nice guy, huh?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:28.320
Or so I thought, until that day.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.430
You take the rice balls to the birds...

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:33.960
...and you'll take them to the Brotherhood.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.380
Thanks as always.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.520
This is Venganto's...

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.030
Your rice ball—

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.600
That's awful! What a jerk!

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.010
Such a petty man.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:19.220
There are times when a man hurts himself
more than the one he is punching.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:20.800
Get out, asshole.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.450
I'm your senior!
How dare you speak to me that way?

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:25.220
This is my lab!

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.140
What happened after that?

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:34.810
Purastelo was immediately exiled
from the Brotherhood by Venganto.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.440
That's the end of the story.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.530
Shall we begin the first-love tasting, then?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:48.040
Based on the information you gave us,
we reproduced the rice ball you ate that day.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.800
Is that water from back then too?

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:56.130
We researched the water standards and
calci usage of the time at the bureau to make this.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.000
Cow's eye?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.080
Calci. Calcium hypochlorite.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.800
Commonly known as
chlorine or bleach powder.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.110
Aroma certainly does have mysterious powers.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:06.250
I feel like I'm about to remember
even things I don't want to.

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:07.220
Excuse me.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:12.120
This is the salt that's dominated
the market since then.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:13.850
Yes.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.280
Can I really eat this?

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.920
Of course.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:20.780
It's been forty years since I last had a rice ball.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.740
Are the memories of your first love
that precious to you?

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:36.960
This isn't it.

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:41.460
It tastes different to the
rice ball I had back then.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.990
What's the matter?

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.050
I see.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.890
So that's it.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.240
Thank you, First Love Sommelier.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.810
Aunty!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.520
Serizawa-san?

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.060
What's going on, Haruta?

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:06.890
After taking just one bite, Serizawa's aunt
declared that the rice ball tasted different.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:09.710
So they failed to replicate
the rice ball from back then?

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:13.370
Of course not. The rice balls
we made are perfectly accurate.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:17.320
Besides, her aunt seemed like
she'd come to terms with something.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:23.590
So this appraisal had another objective
besides recalling her past memories?

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:26.050
That would be the implication, yes.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.120
This is it for us, Chika-chan.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:29.730
Let's go.

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.350
What? But...

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:33.100
We're ten minutes late already.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.520
Oh, practice!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.590
Serizawa-san will be fine.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:39.980
If she needs help, she'll come to us directly.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.600
True that.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.520
She doesn't hold back.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.010
Serizawa-san?

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:05.510
Huh?

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.540
Haruta?

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.070
Um, why are you here this late at night?

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:13.140
We're taking the first train
tomorrow to Hanamaki, Iwate.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.090
Here. Your travel expenses.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.150
You're kidding, right?

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:22.540
We'll stay here tonight and take a taxi
to the station early tomorrow.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.670
It's only a day trip.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.230
You silly goose!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:28.780
Please. You and Kamijou-kun
are the only ones I can ask for help.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.070
Why drag <i>me</i> along, then?

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.050
Did something happen?

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:36.640
My aunt called me and said she's
going to Hanamaki tomorrow.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:37.490
Okay, and?

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.570
Venganto is in Hanamaki.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:42.080
Huh? Weren't his current whereabouts unknown?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.000
Sorry. Client confidentiality.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.640
I can't let her meet that shady man all alone.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.860
We have to get there before her and stop her!

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.970
Still, going to Hanamaki all of a sudden?

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.060
Please come with me.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.430
One ought to help a friend in need, right?

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.020
You made this bed, Chika-chan.
Now we get to lie in it.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:04.170
Jeez, we have practice...

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:07.440
Well, we'd better get to sleep soon.
We're taking the first train, after all.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.090
Chika-chan, could you lay the beds out—

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:09.860
Make your own!

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.100
Homura-san...

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:19.540
Thank you.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:23.010
I was scared to be by myself.

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:24.210
Wanna sleep together?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.710
That's not what I meant.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.600
I know.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:31.690
You know, I was sure there
was nothing you'd be afraid of.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.380
You've got the talent, not to mention the riches.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:38.100
I actually envy you.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.230
Why? Because I have nothing to lose?

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:43.040
Because you're always surrounded by people.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.300
I don't want my aunt to leave me.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:50.180
I don't want to be alone anymore.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:54.050
I've got my own fears, you know.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.400
Of what?

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.700
Nothing. Never mind.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.200
Good night.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.150
I'll wait over there.

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.220
Don't worry.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:21.250
We took the first train, so if we just
wait here, she'll show up eventually.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.940
Let's take this opportunity
to practise, Chika-chan.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:25.910
What, here?

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:29.230
That may help my aunt notice us, too.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:47.790
<i>There aren't many, but it feels so mysterious
having complete strangers listening to us.</i>

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:50.290
<i>My attention is drifting away from my fingertips</i>

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:53.520
<i>and towards Haruta—towards someplace far away.</i>

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:00.770
Aunty!

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:03.670
Naoko? What are you doing here?

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.010
Let's go back.

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:07.550
Nothing good will come of meeting Venganto.

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:10.350
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.860
Naoko dragged you here, didn't she?

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:17.240
We're technically here to protect you
from the clutches of the evil Venganto.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.260
Venganto is a formidable opponent.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.790
For what it's worth, I'll fight too.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:24.710
I don't think you can beat him now.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:29.360
Do you mean it's no longer
possible to meet Venganto?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.550
That's right. He's no longer in this world.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.160
Not just Venganto, either.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:40.080
All the members of the Forest Brotherhood
died of the same illness.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.120
At first, it was just a normal search for a first love.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.810
I found out immediately that he'd passed away.

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:52.790
But I got greedy and requested
further investigations,

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.610
and ended up learning things I would've
been better off not knowing.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.780
What are the odds of the entire Brotherhood
succumbing to the same illness?

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:05.450
Astronomical. Even I knew straight away.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.750
I realised that I, too,
might fall victim to it some day.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.630
That made me so scared
I couldn't sleep at night.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.880
What the...

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:19.510
So when I got the postcard from Asagiri-san,
I came up with this idea.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.580
The purpose of this first love appraisal

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:27.310
was to recreate the salted rice balls from back then
and compare them to your memories.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.320
You thought they were the cause of the illness.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.210
Yes.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:36.690
If the rice balls Asagiri-san made tasted
the same as the ones from back then,

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:43.330
that would've meant that the Brotherhood
was eating ordinary rice balls,

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:47.290
and their cause of death
would've been buried in the dark.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.580
But it was different.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.570
Indeed.

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:55.250
The rice balls Venganto was feeding
to the birds and me were different.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:20:01.800
So the one who served the Brotherhood
poisoned rice balls and caused their deaths

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.050
was Venganto.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.390
What?!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:10.130
On that day, he was trying to stop Purastelo
from eating the poisoned rice balls.

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:15.690
And he tried to protect her by throwing
her out without telling her a thing.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:19.280
But why would he poison the Brotherhood?

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:23.170
Only Venganto knows the answer to that.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:24.920
Vengeance.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.910
It's Esperanto.

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.580
Venganto means "avenger".

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:36.670
That's what he always called
himself when we were alone.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.690
What does Purastelo mean, then?

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.470
Pura Stelo.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.310
A pure star.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.680
First Love Sommelier.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:48.480
Yes?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:52.010
What's your appraisal of my first love?

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:54.310
The certified real deal.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.160
Naoko.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.230
I'm sorry to have worried you.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:00.920
I was afraid of dying.

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.490
Because I wanted to live with you.

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.220
I'm sorry.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.670
But why did Venganto kill himself?

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:19.550
Maybe he couldn't live with the guilt.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:27.090
Are you really going back today?

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:29.560
I can pay for hotel rooms and tickets.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:33.770
We can't skip out on practice any more.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:40.130
<i>The others must be rehearsing hard right now.</i>

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.700
<i>I felt like I was close to something back there,</i>

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:45.110
<i>but looking at the score
only makes me anxious now.</i>

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:51.300
I must be tired.

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:52.710
This isn't like you.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:56.750
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:00.670
I just decided to come along because
I was worried about my attendance.

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.490
Watching you makes me worried sick—

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:05.130
H-Hey!

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:06.320
You're so shy!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:08.220
Shut it!

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:33.170
Give back Kusakabe-sensei!

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:34.760
Sorry to have caused you trouble.

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:36.110
Bring me the gorilla's head.

00:23:36.110 --> 00:23:38.060
The demon of lust...

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:40.940
I'll be Kusakabe-sensei's knight in shining armour!
